  "text": "Second Shift is an AI research agent built specifically for neuroscience. Its task is to distinguish imagined hand and foot movements using recorded EEG. Claude plans the experiments. Our dedicated EEG pipeline filters brain signals, tests electrode configurations, and measures model performance. MongoDB Atlas preserves results and retrieves research notes to guide the next decision. Now watch what happens when we stop the worker during an experiment. When we restart it, completed results are reused and the interrupted experiment runs again. Next, we clear its context and cut the electrode limit from sixty-four to nine. It rebuilds from saved evidence and continues the same neuroscience challenge with fewer sensors. The agent can start over. Your neuroscience research shouldn't have to.",
